# Beam Remote Desktop PAM config
#
# Minimal: auth + account + session. pam_systemd (included via
# common-session on Ubuntu/Debian) registers each desktop session
# with systemd-logind, which is required for FUSE mounts, snap apps,
# and proper /run/user/<uid> management.
#
# No pam_loginuid — the server process is multi-user; each agent
# runs in its own systemd transient service with the correct UID.
# No common-password — Beam doesn't do password changes.

@include common-auth
@include common-account
@include common-session
